# Shared Go rules (cursor-packs)

When generating, completing, or fixing Go:

1. Load `.cursor/skills/golang-quality/SKILL.md` and follow its constraints and quality gates.
2. For deep patterns / anti-patterns, load that skill's `reference.md` (compact examples: `reference-patterns.md`).
3. Prefer project `make format` / `make lint` / `make vet` / `make test` when those targets exist; otherwise use `gofumpt`/`gofmt`, `golangci-lint`, `go vet`, `go test`.
4. For multi-section markdown, reports, or TOC builders: follow `.cursor/rules/go-structured-strings.mdc` (`text/template` over WriteString spaghetti).

When the user asks to review, audit, rate quality, check code, or production readiness of Go:

1. Load `.cursor/skills/review-code-staged/SKILL.md` (stage menu; do not dump all checklists first).
2. Staged review **includes** generation-gate detect as **Stage 8** (same `golang-quality` constraints used while writing, plus `go-structured-strings` for report builders). Prefer including stage 8 when the user wants detect-only full quality.

For export/visibility audits: `.cursor/skills/review-member-visibility/SKILL.md`.

When adding GoReleaser, GitHub Releases, or tag-based Go binary publishing: `.cursor/skills/setup-goreleaser/SKILL.md`.

Project-specific `.cursor/rules/` (architecture, logging, domain) still apply and take precedence for local invariants.

When the user asks for code smells, technical debt, or maintainability review:

1. Load `.cursor/skills/review-code-smells/SKILL.md`.
